                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The patient’s HbA1c is markedly elevated, indicating poor long-term glycemic control and likely uncontrolled diabetes mellitus. This significantly increases the risk for microvascular and macrovascular complications. Clinical correlation and prompt optimization of diabetes management are strongly recommended.</td>
